
Nice, you’re basically inventing **“Royale Credit”** – a single system that can:

* Front players premium stuff now
* Let them “pay it off” by **skill**, **grind**, or **cash**
* Scale risk/reward via a **credit score**

Let’s merge all 3 into *one* clean model you could actually implement.

---

## 1. One unified concept: **Advance Contracts**

Name for players:

> **Advance Contracts** – “Get premium rewards early, complete the contract to keep them.”

Internally: every “loan” is just a **Contract** object with three axes:

1. **What you’re advancing** (Principal)

   * Premium Pass / Season Track
   * Card upgrades / power boosts
   * Cosmetics / access to special modes

2. **How they earn it** (Conditions)

   * **Skill** milestones (rank, wins, crowns)
   * **Engagement** milestones (daily logins, games played, quests)
   * **Hybrid** (player choice or system-chosen mix)

3. **How risky / generous it is** (Credit Tier)

   * Tied to a **Player Credit Score**
   * Higher tier = bigger advances + softer penalties

So the 3 variations become:

* **Variation A (Skill)** → “Performance Contract”
* **Variation B (Engagement)** → “Grind Contract”
* **Variation C (Credit Score)** → “Credit Tier” that scales the first two

All powered by the same underlying data model.

---

## 2. Data model for the unified system

You could literally model everything like:

### 2.1. Player Credit Profile

```pseudo
PlayerCreditProfile {
  player_id
  credit_score        // 0–100 or E/D/C/B/A/S
  trust_tier          // Bronze / Silver / Gold / Platinum
  total_contracts     // number ever taken
  successful_contracts
  failed_contracts
  last_contract_end   // timestamp
}
```

* **credit_score** goes up when they complete contracts, down when they fail.
* **trust_tier** is a discretized version of the score (Bronze, Silver, Gold…).
* Used to gate:

  * Max principal value
  * Max contracts per season
  * Interest size / penalty severity

---

### 2.2. Generic Advance Contract

```pseudo
AdvanceContract {
  contract_id
  player_id

  contract_type          // "PASS", "UPGRADE", "COSMETIC", "ACCESS"
  reward_package_id      // look up what they get

  // Timing
  start_time
  end_time

  // Conditions (all optional, you can combine)
  required_rank          // e.g. Gold League
  required_wins          // e.g. 50 wins this season
  required_crowns        // e.g. 200 crowns
  required_play_days     // e.g. 10 unique days
  required_matches       // e.g. 100 matches
  required_quests        // e.g. complete 15 daily quests

  // Outcomes
  success_rewards        // what becomes permanent
  failure_penalties      // what’s revoked / nerfed
  failure_options        // e.g. "PAY_GEMS", "HARD_QUEST", "FORFEIT"

  // Economy
  principal_value        // internal $ value of the loaned package
  expected_ARPU_impact   // for analytics
  interest_soft_currency // gold fee, if any
  interest_hard_currency // gem fee, if any

  status                 // ACTIVE, SUCCEEDED, FAILED, SETTLED
  progress_state         // cached counters for UI
}
```

Everything you want (A/B/C) is just different **parameter sets** for this one object.

