## 3. How the **three variations** live inside this model

### 3.1. Variation A – **Performance Contract (Skill-based loan)**

* `contract_type`: usually `"PASS"` or `"UPGRADE"`
* Key condition fields:

  * `required_rank`, `required_wins`, `required_crowns`
* Example template:

```pseudo
PerformanceContractTemplate {
  name: "Advance Gold Pass"
  contract_type: "PASS"
  duration_days: 28

  required_rank: "Gold League"
  required_wins: 80
  required_crowns: 200

  failure_options: ["PAY_GEMS", "FORFEIT_FINAL_REWARDS"]
}
```

**How it uses credit score:**

* Bronze: smaller goal (e.g. Silver League), fewer rewards
* Gold: bigger pass, but maybe only rank OR wins required
* Platinum: huge pass, generous conditions, low “interest”

---

### 3.2. Variation B – **Grind Contract (Engagement loan)**

* `contract_type`: usually `"UPGRADE"` or `"ACCESS"`
* Key condition fields:

  * `required_play_days`, `required_matches`, `required_quests`
* Example template:

```pseudo
GrindContractTemplate {
  name: "Upgrade Bundle Advance"
  contract_type: "UPGRADE"
  duration_days: 14

  required_play_days: 10
  required_matches: 120
  required_quests: 12

  failure_options: ["PAY_GEMS", "EXTRA_QUEST_CHAIN"]
}
```

**How it uses credit score:**

* Low-tier players: lower daily demands (e.g., 5 days / 60 matches)
* High-tier: more demanding grind, but **bigger upgrade bundle** upfront

---

### 3.3. Variation C – **Credit Tier (Loyalty-based scaling)**

You don’t make “credit” its own contract; you use it to **scale all contracts**:

Example tiers:

| Tier   | Credit Score | Max Active Contracts | Max Principal per Season | Interest Style                  | Penalty Style                          |
| ------ | ------------ | -------------------- | ------------------------ | ------------------------------- | -------------------------------------- |
| Bronze | 0–20         | 1                    | Small (e.g. $3 value)    | None or very low soft-currency  | Mild: lose some rewards, no shaming    |
| Silver | 21–50        | 2                    | Medium (e.g. $10 value)  | Soft-currency + tiny gem option | Medium: minor gem fee or downgrade     |
| Gold   | 51–80        | 3                    | Large (e.g. $25 value)   | Mostly time-based, low gem fee  | Can lose some perks; cooldown on fail  |
| Plat   | 81–100+      | 4                    | Very large (e.g. $50+)   | Very low interest, flexible     | Gentle: mainly cooldown, no heavy loss |

Credit score updates:

* **On success:**

  * `credit_score += small_bonus + bonus_by_difficulty`
  * Count `successful_contracts++`
* **On fail & settle:**

  * `credit_score -= penalty_based_on_severity`
  * `failed_contracts++`
  * Maybe temporary “loan cooldown” flag

